      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $(-\\infty ,2]?$  You may assume that all points of discontinuity for each function are shown.",
      "worked_solution": "The correct answer is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14262965/assets/7afb04e0197b44ffadeee53bc365910f7c578eb8a3f2e2971a83f4f51947a3af.png)\n\nWe see that $q(x)$ is continuous on the interval $(-\\infty ,3],$ and since $(-\\infty ,2]$ lies completely inside $(-\\infty ,3],$ it is also continuous on $(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are not continuous at $x=-1$, and so are not continuous on $(-\\infty ,2].$\n\n- $p(x)$ and $h(x)$ are not continuous at $x=0$, and so are not continuous on $(-\\infty ,2].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
